WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.825 --> 00:00:15.047
Columbus took Mandy to his cabin.

2
00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:18.149
"You will be safe here," he said.

3
00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:23.473
Curious, Mandy picked up a round metal object.

4
00:00:24.654 --> 00:00:27.677
Its pointy, moving hands were like a clock's.

5
00:00:27.697 --> 00:00:30.239
"What's this?"

6
00:00:30.979 --> 00:00:31.740
asked Mandy.

7
00:00:32.988 --> 00:00:35.810
"It's an astrolabe," explained Columbus.

8
00:00:36.851 --> 00:00:39.353
"It measures the height of the sun from the horizon.

9
00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:42.635
It helps us know where we are on the ocean."

10
00:00:43.956 --> 00:00:47.858
Columbus took the astrolabe and said, "I have to go now.

11
00:00:48.519 --> 00:00:49.019
Stay here."

12
00:00:52.722 --> 00:00:55.223
Meanwhile, Vinnie was getting hungry.

13
00:00:56.404 --> 00:00:58.726
A sailor's life wasn't much fun.

14
00:00:58.746 --> 00:01:04.030
"We're all going to starve," said an old sailor nearby.

15
00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:07.753
"Monsters will eat us before we starve!"

16
00:01:08.453 --> 00:01:09.434
screamed another.

17
00:01:09.454 --> 00:01:12.237
"I want to go home!"

18
00:01:12.897 --> 00:01:13.618
thought Vinnie.

19
00:01:14.859 --> 00:01:17.081
Manuel was tying a knot in a rope.

20
00:01:18.522 --> 00:01:23.366
Another boy was standing by a large coil of rope, holding an hourglass.

21
00:01:24.867 --> 00:01:30.452
When the sand emptied into the bottom, the boy cried: "One glass is gone.

22
00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.561
Now the second begins!"

23
00:01:33.662 --> 00:01:34.642
"What's he doing?"

24
00:01:35.203 --> 00:01:36.464
Vinnie asked Manuel.

25
00:01:36.484 --> 00:01:40.186
"We take turns turning over the hourglass.

26
00:01:41.227 --> 00:01:45.890
Each time it empties, a half hour has gone by," explained Manuel.

27
00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:51.294
"After eight turns, or four hours, another boy takes over."

28
00:01:52.615 --> 00:01:56.057
The boy called to Vinnie, "Hey, take over a minute, will you?"

29
00:01:57.378 --> 00:01:59.700
He put the hourglass into Vinnie's hands.

30
00:02:01.032 --> 00:02:03.933
"It's the second half of the hour," said the boy.

31
00:02:05.073 --> 00:02:07.574
He ran off before Vinnie could protest.

32
00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:10.455
"Here," said Manuel.

33
00:02:11.475 --> 00:02:14.896
He took a biscuit out of his pocket and gave it to Vinnie.

34
00:02:16.076 --> 00:02:20.598
Biscuits were used to mark the time after each turn of the hourglass.

35
00:02:21.758 --> 00:02:23.639
Vinnie thought he was supposed to eat it.

36
00:02:23.659 --> 00:02:28.520
"Ow!" cried Vinnie, after he tried to bite it.

37
00:02:29.416 --> 00:02:33.197
The biscuit was so hard that Vinnie put it down on the ropes.

38
00:02:34.457 --> 00:02:37.918
Meanwhile, Mandy sat alone in the captain's cabin.

39
00:02:39.079 --> 00:02:41.719
The cabin boy had left her a biscuit to eat.

40
00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.380
She put it in her pocket.

41
00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:47.961
Suddenly, there was a loud boom.

42
00:02:49.241 --> 00:02:51.102
Mandy, ran out onto the deck.

43
00:02:51.122 --> 00:02:53.743
"What was that?"

44
00:02:54.463 --> 00:02:55.203
she shouted.

45
00:02:55.223 --> 00:02:57.404
"It's the Pinta!"

46
00:02:57.804 --> 00:02:58.704
cried someone.

47
00:02:59.916 --> 00:03:00.997
"The ship needs help!"

48
00:03:02.318 --> 00:03:09.965
At that moment, she heard a familiar voice shouting, "One glass is gone, and now the second begins!"

49
00:03:09.985 --> 00:03:14.108
"Vinnie!" she cried happily.

50
00:03:14.128 --> 00:03:18.011
"Mandy! Am I glad to see you!"

51
00:03:18.692 --> 00:03:20.534
he exclaimed when she ran up.

52
00:03:21.755 --> 00:03:24.317
He put the hourglass on top of the ropes.

53
00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:26.699
"What are you doing?"

54
00:03:27.359 --> 00:03:27.900
she asked.

55
00:03:29.368 --> 00:03:32.911
"Every thirty minutes, I turn this hourglass over.

56
00:03:34.332 --> 00:03:37.234
Each time, Manuel brings a biscuit.

57
00:03:38.574 --> 00:03:41.717
They're so hard I can't eat them," said Vinnie.

58
00:03:41.737 --> 00:03:44.038
"Don't eat them!"

59
00:03:44.679 --> 00:03:47.160
Mandy shouted, pulling out the photo.

60
00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:49.702
"We need them!

61
00:03:50.122 --> 00:03:53.865
See?" The photo was glowing blue.

62
00:03:53.885 --> 00:03:56.927
"But there are only two biscuits!"

63
00:03:57.447 --> 00:03:58.148
cried Vinnie.

64
00:03:59.488 --> 00:04:01.030
"We need three to go home."

65
00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:06.955
"Don't worry," said Mandy, pulling the biscuit from her pocket.

66
00:04:08.456 --> 00:04:10.978
Mandy placed it next to the other biscuits.

67
00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:15.122
In the photo, the hourglass glowed red.

68
00:04:15.142 --> 00:04:19.026
"I'm so glad we're leaving!"

69
00:04:19.546 --> 00:04:20.307
cried Vinnie.

70
00:04:21.608 --> 00:04:25.812
The children closed their eyes and fell down the dark tunnel.
